{title: Oceans (Where Feet May Fail) (FJ_116_en)}
{subtitle: Meer}
{song_number: 116}
{language: en}
{tempo: 60}
{time: 4/4}
{key: D}
{composer: Joel Houston, Matt Crocker, Salomon Ligthelm}
{lyricist: Joel Houston, Matt Crocker, Salomon Ligthelm}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[Bm]You call me out upon the [A/C#]wa[D]ters,
the great un[A]known where feet may [G]fail.
[Bm]And there I find You [A/C#]in the [D]myst'ry,
in oceans [A]deep, my faith will [G]stand.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[G]And I will [D]call upon Your [A]name,
[G]and keep my [D]eyes above the [A]waves.
When oceans [G]rise, my soul will [D]rest
in Your em[A]brace, for I am [G]Yours
and [A]You are [Bm]mine.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[Bm]Your grace abounds in [A/C#]deepest [D]waters,
Your sov'reign [A]hand will be my [G]guide.
[Bm]Where feet may fail and [A/C#]fear sur[D]rounds me,
You've never [A]failed and You won't start [G]now.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[G]And I will [D]call upon Your [A]name,
[G]and keep my [D]eyes above the [A]waves.
When oceans [G]rise, my soul will [D]rest
in Your em[A]brace, for I am [G]Yours
and [A]You are [Bm]mine.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge}
[Bm]Spirit lead me where my trust is [G]without borders,
let me walk u[D]pon the water
wherever You would [A]call me.
[Bm]Take me deeper than my feet [G]could ever wander,
and my faith [D]will be made stronger
in the presence of my [A]Saviour.
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus}
[G]And I will [D]call upon Your [A]name,
[G]and keep my [D]eyes above the [A]waves.
When oceans [G]rise, my soul will [D]rest
in Your em[A]brace, for I am [G]Yours
and [A]You are [Bm]mine.
{end_of_chorus}